1
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:05,982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

2
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:11,362
<i>Let's just not have the baby.</i>

3
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:14,824
<i>What if Ae-sun dies during childbirth?</i>
<i>We shouldn't let her do that!</i>

4
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:17,327
<i>Just wait until the baby is born.</i>

5
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:19,162
<i>You'll be even more annoying.</i>

6
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:26,377
{\an8}Remember, you have to
support her head like this.

7
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:29,881
{\an8}Uh, no.
I don't think I want to.

8
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:32,425
I shouldn't.

9
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:34,177
I think I'll hurt her.

10
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,429
You just have to be careful.

11
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:40,183
Honey?

12
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:43,770
The baby. She's a bit…

13
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:47,565
A bit strange looking?

14
00:01:48,191 --> 00:01:50,026
She's all wrinkly, huh?

15
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:53,113
Look at her nostrils.

16
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,989
We can fit a cotton swab in there.

17
00:01:55,865 --> 00:01:58,201
She's just so… little.

18
00:01:58,284 --> 00:01:59,369
So little.

19
00:02:00,036 --> 00:02:01,871
How will she make it in this world?

20
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:04,249
A dog could run in and snatch her up.

21
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:08,169
What are you so worried about? What?

22
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:10,046
You're the Steelheart.

23
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:15,051
We'll be there to protect her.

24
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:20,056
She'll always have us.

25
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:24,269
Oh, she smiled!

26
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:27,939
<i>All those years ago,</i>
<i>my parents couldn't have known…</i>

27
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:31,276
<i>What?</i>

28
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:34,404
<i>…just how long I'd be in their debt.</i>

29
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:40,660
<i>Who are you anyway?</i>

30
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:43,371
This isn't like you at all.

31
00:02:43,454 --> 00:02:45,582
You hate it when I pack things up for you.

32
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:50,086
Should I not take the tangerines
just because you want them?

33
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:56,676
Your husband, has he lost his job?

34
00:02:57,468 --> 00:02:59,762
Of course not. Why would you think that?

35
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:03,600
When you're pinching pennies,
fruit is always the first thing to go.

36
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:05,602
Fine, I won't take them.

37
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:11,191
Why can't we visit your new place?
We still haven't seen it.

38
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:13,610
Just come. It's fine.

39
00:03:14,944 --> 00:03:16,571
I'll come tomorrow, then.

40
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:18,364
You have so much luggage to carry.

41
00:03:18,448 --> 00:03:21,868
Actually, uh, tomorrow's not great.
I'm busy.

42
00:03:21,951 --> 00:03:24,204
Well, busy or not, I'm coming over.

43
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,622
What's the rush?

44
00:03:26,664 --> 00:03:27,874
What's wrong?

45
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:33,254
You can't fool me.

46
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:36,216
How you're acting right now
is just like Eun-myeong.

47
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:39,385
When he asked me not to visit his school,
there was a reason.

48
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:44,265
Tomorrow, I wanna see
what it is for myself.

49
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:45,934
We don't have room for you.

50
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:49,437
There's no room for you to come over.

51
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:52,815
Why not?

52
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:56,027
Uh, it's a one-bedroom.

53
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:00,490
I quit my job.

54
00:04:05,286 --> 00:04:08,289
I started a business,
and I put up everything.

55
00:04:09,874 --> 00:04:11,084
I'm all in.

56
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:14,629
Oh, Mother, who knew
Geum-myeong could get reckless?

57
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:17,423
Maybe Eun-myeong is passing
his baton to his sister.

58
00:04:18,007 --> 00:04:20,468
Wait, what? But why?

59
00:04:21,052 --> 00:04:22,428
Why did you quit your job?

60
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:31,187
What happened to your hand?

61
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:33,398
What happened? What?

62
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:36,526
Everyone get out! Get out!

63
00:04:36,609 --> 00:04:39,988
If none of you are going to listen to me,
then just get out!

64
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:41,864
But I'm injured.

65
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:44,367
I told you a hundred times
about that uncle in Hallim

66
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:47,078
who had to have his fingers amputated
because of frostbite.

67
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:49,330
"Wear gloves.
Wear gloves when you're handling ice."

68
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:51,374
I was like a broken record!

69
00:04:51,457 --> 00:04:53,042
You never listen, do you?

70
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:57,130
Your uncle Jong-gu
always has new business ideas,

71
00:04:57,213 --> 00:04:59,507
and he has to ask me for money
just to survive.

72
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:03,219
Mom, do you even care
what kind of business it is?

73
00:05:04,762 --> 00:05:07,724
I've never been the one
to cause problems for this family, have I?

74
00:05:07,807 --> 00:05:10,685
- I can hear you.
- Now, for the first time in my life…

75
00:05:11,227 --> 00:05:13,229
What about kids? Are you not having kids?

76
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:16,357
I knew
you were gonna say that again.

77
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:18,318
You think you're fine
because you're still young.

78
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:20,153
But when you get older
and start getting sick,

79
00:05:20,236 --> 00:05:21,404
what will you do without--

80
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:23,990
What, Mom? Did you have kids
just so you can have a nurse?

81
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:25,616
Hyeon-suk already has two children!

82
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:26,993
And what future do they have?

83
00:05:27,076 --> 00:05:28,619
I can still hear you.

84
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:30,538
You think kids just grow up
all up on their own?

85
00:05:30,621 --> 00:05:32,457
Do you have any idea what a kid costs now?

86
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,167
You think only rich people raise children?

87
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:35,084
I don't.

88
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:38,296
I just don't want to have children
I can't provide for.

89
00:05:38,379 --> 00:05:40,298
I want to buy them
new clothes every season.

90
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:42,008
I want to buy them shoes
that actually fit.

91
00:05:42,091 --> 00:05:45,428
I want to pay for piano lessons,
for ballet, their first studio apartment!

92
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:47,096
I don't have money, and I had kids.

93
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:49,682
Look, Hyeon-suk's family
bought all this stuff, didn't they?

94
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:52,143
Che-il has one grandpa
with money at least!

95
00:06:10,036 --> 00:06:11,954
Did you come here
to pick a fight?

96
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,709
Rolling around
at rock bottom is draining.

97
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:19,087
Everything's just
really difficult right now.

98
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:20,713
<i>Their son had frostbite,</i>

99
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:24,175
<i>and their daughter had downsized</i>
<i>to a studio apartment.</i>

100
00:06:25,385 --> 00:06:26,594
<i>But in the end</i>…

101
00:06:26,677 --> 00:06:29,097
Our troubles
are never going to end.

102
00:06:29,722 --> 00:06:31,182
Will they?

103
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:33,142
What's happening?

104
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:34,435
Where did we go wrong?

105
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:37,188
<i>…it was those words from my poor mother…</i>

106
00:06:37,271 --> 00:06:38,356
Oh God!

107
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:40,483
<i>…that made my father take a risk.</i>

108
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,527
Goddammit.

109
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:45,363
I'm sick of this.

110
00:06:46,155 --> 00:06:48,616
<i>The first risk</i>
<i>my dad ever took…</i>

111
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:52,370
<i>was launched from a bazooka.</i>

112
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:54,914
I hear your daughter
is also starting a business.

113
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:57,166
She needs a backup somewhere.

114
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:58,626
Do it for your family.

115
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:10,346
That's it! You've lost your mind!

116
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:12,432
How could you do something so reckless?

117
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:15,601
Any idiot can tell
something's fishy about this.

118
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:20,022
The moment I heard you sold
the cabbage field, I got suspicious.

119
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:22,817
Some company chairman
is building a vacation home.

120
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:26,404
You want us to believe
the money just fell into your lap one day?

121
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:28,531
- Not buying it.
- What the hell's out here anyway?

122
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:31,617
Who on earth runs a store
in the middle of nowhere?

123
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:34,954
Great, if there are no people to feed,
there's always the wild dogs.

124
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:39,000
I heard a golf course is being built here.

125
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:41,544
Golf course?
Well, isn't that lucky for you.

126
00:07:41,627 --> 00:07:42,587
What a coincidence.

127
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,922
Haven't you seen
those investigation shows?

128
00:07:45,506 --> 00:07:47,258
When people are scamming you,

129
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:49,927
everything they say
sounds too good to be true.

130
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:53,055
You wanna be homeless
at your age?

131
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:56,601
Who puts up their house
to buy a commercial building at 50?

132
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:59,437
If he can't do it at 50,
he'll never do it at all.

133
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:02,356
If he wants to take a risk,
better late than never.

134
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:04,484
I'm proud of you.

135
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:07,570
Even if we show up
and the building turns out to be haunted,

136
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:09,822
even if there's no building there at all,

137
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:13,284
we're sticking this out together,
Gwan-Sik.

138
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:15,620
The loyalty between these two…

139
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:17,788
It's certainly something to behold,
all right.

140
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:20,750
My head.

141
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:23,419
Tell him to pull over and let me out.

142
00:08:38,476 --> 00:08:40,228
Look at all these banners.

143
00:08:41,562 --> 00:08:42,939
Which is it?

144
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:43,940
Huh?

145
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:46,400
Oh my.

146
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:47,318
Wait a minute.

147
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:51,489
What are all these buildings
doing way out here?

148
00:08:51,572 --> 00:08:54,408
Oh my. A hospital, a clinic,

149
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:57,537
a supermarket, and a specialty restaurant.

150
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,372
PREMIUM COMMERCIAL PROPERTY
WITH EVERYTHING

151
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:01,040
RENTAL INQUIRY FOR COMMERCIAL PROPERTY

152
00:09:10,716 --> 00:09:14,762
If they ever build that golf course,
even Park Se-ri might come in here.

153
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:18,891
Well, if she does,
meeting her will be one more thing

154
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:20,560
you can thank your son for.

155
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:23,437
By the way,
you both own this place, right?

156
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:26,357
It's good to know
my family name is on something.

157
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:29,694
Are you still angry
over these old issues?

158
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:31,779
Is this about the boat we had?

159
00:09:31,862 --> 00:09:33,990
'Cause I said
it belonged to the Oh family?

160
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:38,202
Whoever bought it, it was nice
to see him riding in that boat.

161
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:42,123
You can guess how it felt

162
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:46,002
when I heard my son had gone
from a captain to a manual laborer.

163
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:50,089
I know you've been married to him
practically for your entire life,

164
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:51,632
but he's the only son I have.

165
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:55,428
Seeing him suffer
just breaks my heart to pieces.

166
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:58,472
I'm sorry, Mother.

167
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:00,933
I took your precious son away from you,

168
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:03,644
and he's suffered ever since.

169
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:07,023
Well, there's no need to be sorry. Uh…

170
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:10,151
Tell me, I'm curious.

171
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:13,696
Do you remember everything from the past?

172
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:15,406
Everything about your son,

173
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:18,743
like the way he always chose me over you.

174
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:20,703
I mean…

175
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:21,912
Oh, you know.

176
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:24,624
That time when I slapped you.

177
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:26,375
It only happened once.

178
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:30,087
You're not still upset about that,
are you?

179
00:10:30,963 --> 00:10:32,840
How could I ever forget such a thing?

180
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:36,510
That was the very first
I had ever been slapped by anybody.

181
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:39,055
It's okay.

182
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:41,515
You made up for it.

183
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:46,020
How did I do that?
I've never done a thing for you.

184
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:48,814
It was when we

185
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,233
lost Dong-myeong.

186
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:55,279
You never once blamed me, and you…

187
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:58,783
you didn't criticize me either
for any of it.

188
00:10:59,867 --> 00:11:02,370
When a cow's lost its calf,
you don't put a yolk on it.

189
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:06,624
I went to your house early in the mornings
just to check up on you.

190
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:17,385
I still have that golden toad,
the one you stole when you ran away.

191
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:21,013
I'll give it to you instead of Gyeong-ok.

192
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:23,641
I'm sorry I was so hard on you.

193
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:25,935
Consider it a thank-you present
for moving on.

194
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:31,107
I guess my mother-in-law
is a cut above your mother-in-law.

195
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:33,192
Way above.

196
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:43,786
COMMERCIAL LEASE AGREEMENT

197
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:50,668
LESSEE NAME: PARK YEONG-RAN

198
00:11:57,299 --> 00:12:00,678
<i>Meanwhile,</i>
<i>there was someone else firing a bazooka.</i>

199
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:16,026
Jesus.

200
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:18,279
You been going crazy
with the sweets lately?

201
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:20,990
What are you gonna do
about all that weight?

202
00:12:21,073 --> 00:12:24,577
People go into business
with pretty realtors, not fatties.

203
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:30,583
See these bikes here?
We'll get rid of that belly in no time.

204
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:33,502
Plus, I've heard
when couples do things together,

205
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:36,547
it tends to strengthen the relationship.

206
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:39,258
Did ping-pong strengthen
your relationship with that woman?

207
00:12:39,341 --> 00:12:43,429
I told you it was a mixed league, okay?
It's actually very common.

208
00:12:43,512 --> 00:12:45,890
Is that why you chose
Mi-suk for real estate?

209
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:47,975
Fine, th… then don't ride the bike.

210
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:50,102
I'm doing a nice thing for you.

211
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:53,272
Fine.

212
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:55,858
I'll try it.

213
00:12:57,443 --> 00:12:59,361
We'll take a ride around the block.

214
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:01,906
Woo-hoo!

215
00:13:04,784 --> 00:13:07,703
Oh!

216
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:10,206
Yeah.

217
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:12,625
Yeah.

218
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:15,795
Look! I still got it! See?

219
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:17,963
Check me out!

220
00:13:19,256 --> 00:13:21,091
See?

221
00:13:23,677 --> 00:13:24,720
Whoo!

222
00:13:33,395 --> 00:13:34,230
Figures.

223
00:13:34,814 --> 00:13:37,233
He won't ride next to me. He never has.

224
00:13:37,733 --> 00:13:41,070
Hey! Hurry up!
This is a cycling course.

225
00:13:41,153 --> 00:13:42,863
You understand what cycling means?

226
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:46,033
Go fast!

227
00:13:46,116 --> 00:13:49,078
Hey, look. Go up ahead.
The view here is just…

228
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:51,080
I mean, wow! Oh!

229
00:13:57,878 --> 00:13:59,547
Where do you think you're going?

230
00:14:00,965 --> 00:14:02,049
Huh?

231
00:14:02,132 --> 00:14:03,259
- Whoa!
- Go away.

232
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:05,427
Where do you think you're going?

233
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:08,389
You can't just ride past me like that.

234
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:09,723
Shit, uh…

235
00:14:10,432 --> 00:14:12,518
Wow! I wonder why she ran out to see you.

236
00:14:12,601 --> 00:14:14,395
Huh? Who's that?

237
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:18,607
Hmm. I see you found a new playmate.

238
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:20,526
Look, babe,

239
00:14:21,151 --> 00:14:22,778
go back inside and make your <i>jeon.</i>

240
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:23,696
Hmm.

241
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:29,660
Why'd you agree to a bike ride
in the first place?

242
00:14:30,452 --> 00:14:31,996
Was that your way of saying goodbye?

243
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:35,040
Well, I suppose I did it
because, after 30 years of marriage,

244
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:37,293
we'd never been around
the neighborhood together once.

245
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:39,461
Is this because of Mom's tangerine field?

246
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:41,547
Are you selling it
to start a real estate business?

247
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:44,842
Exactly. I don't need your money
to eat anymore.

248
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:48,137
You just have to ruin everything,
don't you?

249
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:50,973
After all the effort
I put in to make it work, you just--

250
00:14:51,056 --> 00:14:51,891
Am I a dog?

251
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:55,603
Do you think after all these years
of keeping me cooped up at home

252
00:14:55,686 --> 00:14:57,438
while you had fun all around town,

253
00:14:58,022 --> 00:14:59,648
one bike ride would fix it?

254
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:02,651
How dare you!

255
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:09,283
When the kids come back,

256
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:12,578
tell them to pick up
the rest of their shoes.

257
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:15,414
Or else I can throw them away.

258
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:18,083
I don't know why
they left all these pairs behind.

259
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:34,350
Okay, okay.

260
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:37,353
All right, I see what you're doing.
I see it.

261
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:39,563
Don't put on a show.

262
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:43,317
Well, it's not a show.

263
00:15:44,234 --> 00:15:45,903
And you know that, Sang-gil.

264
00:15:55,079 --> 00:15:57,998
I put food on the table for this family,
and this is what I get?

265
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:00,084
A runaway for a daughter.

266
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:03,712
Now, I have to take time out of
my crazy schedule to go hunt you down.

267
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:07,257
Did you put back my bedroom door?
I need my privacy!

268
00:16:10,427 --> 00:16:13,263
Good Lord. How the hell did I end up
with a kid like you anyway?

269
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:16,433
Before you, we never had
a troublemaker in the family.

270
00:16:17,518 --> 00:16:19,937
Oh-seong, if you beat up Eun-myeong
one more time,

271
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,438
I'm taking you all to court!

272
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:25,317
- You goddamn brat!
- Knock it off!

273
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:27,611
So proud of my whole family today!

274
00:16:32,449 --> 00:16:34,451
SANG-GIL LOVES OK

275
00:16:39,915 --> 00:16:41,834
Do you really like this boy that much?

276
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:47,965
Dear, this is your first love, isn't it?

277
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:51,135
"First love"? Who cares?
Don't encourage her now!

278
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:52,594
Can you please act like a mother?

279
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:56,473
At least you get to experience it.
I never did.

280
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:17,745
{\an8}So you really never loved me?
Not even for a little while?

281
00:17:18,495 --> 00:17:22,332
If I had loved you,
I would've lost my mind long ago.

282
00:17:22,916 --> 00:17:23,792
Remember,

283
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:28,338
after I gave birth to Hyeon-suk, you were
seeing that woman from the bathhouse.

284
00:17:28,422 --> 00:17:30,758
We used to be in the same class at school.
That's all.

285
00:17:30,841 --> 00:17:32,718
I thought you went to school in Seoul.

286
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:33,761
How dare you.

287
00:17:33,844 --> 00:17:36,930
When I found out about the affair,
I raised hell.

288
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:39,391
You threw a clothes hanger at me.

289
00:17:39,475 --> 00:17:42,227
I didn't throw it at you.
You ran at me and bumped into it.

290
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:43,854
Since then,

291
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:46,148
I've had no tears left to cry.

292
00:17:46,648 --> 00:17:49,818
When a woman's heart is
beaten down enough, she stops feeling.

293
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:53,489
People tell me I'm a saint, but I'm not.

294
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:56,825
Not loving you was
the only way I survived.

295
00:17:59,995 --> 00:18:01,872
- Honey.
- Don't even try.

296
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:05,209
- Honey.
- Save your breath.

297
00:18:05,709 --> 00:18:09,922
You know, Hyeon-suk has asthma
because you always smoked in front of her.

298
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:14,968
When I listened to you refuse her
the money she needed to save her husband,

299
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:17,679
any sentiment I had left for you

300
00:18:18,597 --> 00:18:20,307
disappeared from my heart forever.

301
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:21,725
Oh shit.

302
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:23,936
Do I really have to do this?

303
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:26,230
Do you know how humiliating this is?

304
00:18:26,313 --> 00:18:29,483
I would say your life has been
pretty good so far.

305
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:34,863
All I want now is
the chance to enjoy the rest of mine.

306
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:40,077
Please just let me go.

307
00:18:41,411 --> 00:18:45,207
After all,
I did my best to raise your children.

308
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:49,294
JEJU DISTRICT COURT

309
00:18:56,426 --> 00:18:57,511
Goddammit.

310
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:08,438
We don't have to change cars right now.

311
00:19:19,074 --> 00:19:22,327
How come you never told me
you recognized my shoe that day?

312
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,331
Why does that matter now?

313
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:39,303
That woman's fleeing
with her child.

314
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:42,598
Look, they're like refugees from the war,
aren't they?

315
00:19:42,681 --> 00:19:44,516
Get a picture of that woman!

316
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,851
Get a picture of her now!

317
00:20:00,282 --> 00:20:01,366
How dare she.

318
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,453
She's been out dancing?

319
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:12,878
If I had busted you for dancing,
you would have left right then and there.

320
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:18,675
You would've raised hell
and left me on the spot.

321
00:20:32,773 --> 00:20:33,982
I'm not even smiling.

322
00:20:34,066 --> 00:20:37,402
You were always so cold to me.
I nearly froze to death.

323
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:04,554
What do you want, punk?
I don't have any money to give you.

324
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:06,056
Jesus.

325
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:08,976
My wife thought you'd need that.

326
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:15,315
She was right.

327
00:21:15,399 --> 00:21:17,442
INSTANT RICE

328
00:21:17,526 --> 00:21:18,568
Goddammit.

329
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:21,697
She did dodge the bullet.

330
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:22,864
<i>Out of my way!</i>

331
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:25,367
Why you little… How dare you!

332
00:21:25,450 --> 00:21:29,246
Why don't you come to your senses first,
Bu Sang-gil?

333
00:21:29,329 --> 00:21:30,414
You hear me?

334
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:33,000
And then we'll find out
who dodged whose bullet!

335
00:21:33,083 --> 00:21:34,126
How dare you!

336
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:39,089
<i>Why is it so surprising</i>

337
00:21:39,172 --> 00:21:43,176
<i>when, one day, we reap</i>
<i>what we've so relentlessly sown?</i>

338
00:21:43,677 --> 00:21:46,596
GEUMEUNDONG'S

339
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,473
If this goes south,

340
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:50,517
we're losing our apartment.

341
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:56,732
Not in a thousand years would I ever dream
you'd throw me a curveball like this.

342
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:03,322
So then why didn't you try
to talk me out of it?

343
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:06,783
Well,

344
00:22:07,576 --> 00:22:10,245
…when you first told me
that you wanted to buy this store,

345
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:15,375
{\an8}<i>I realized it's been 30 years</i>
<i>since I saw that look on your face.</i>

346
00:22:15,459 --> 00:22:17,544
So if you're scared, Gwan-sik,
walk away now.

347
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:19,421
Just go back home.

348
00:22:20,047 --> 00:22:23,633
In all… 19 years of my life, Ae-sun…

349
00:22:27,387 --> 00:22:29,014
I've never felt more excited.

350
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:34,478
You haven't been so excited in 30 years.

351
00:22:34,561 --> 00:22:35,854
How can I ruin that?

352
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:40,817
Still, I don't know what made you try
something you've never done before.

353
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:42,361
Was it Geum-myeong's business?

354
00:22:43,236 --> 00:22:44,905
Or maybe Eun-myeong's hand?

355
00:22:46,573 --> 00:22:48,325
I realized if I never tried,

356
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,828
I would be proving what you said about me.

357
00:22:52,662 --> 00:22:56,333
Listen, living with you, that would be
too much of a gamble for me.

358
00:23:01,129 --> 00:23:03,256
I wanted our life to be halfway decent.

359
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:05,092
Just never seems to work out.

360
00:23:05,926 --> 00:23:08,637
I feel like it's my fault
that our kids are struggling.

361
00:23:09,262 --> 00:23:10,180
I hate that.

362
00:23:15,102 --> 00:23:16,436
It's not true what people say.

363
00:23:17,396 --> 00:23:19,022
They say money isn't everything.

364
00:23:19,523 --> 00:23:20,816
But we all know it is.

365
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:24,444
We even need money
to do something for our grandkids.

366
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:26,488
Che-il gets pajamas from Sang-gil,

367
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:30,534
and they're always better quality pajamas
than anything I could get him. Always!

368
00:23:31,576 --> 00:23:34,788
Listen, if I could go back 30 years,

369
00:23:36,623 --> 00:23:39,376
I would choose to run away with you again.

370
00:23:39,459 --> 00:23:41,294
If I hadn't gone with you,

371
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:43,755
I wouldn't be a restaurant owner today.

372
00:23:46,007 --> 00:23:47,342
Unbelievable, right?

373
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:49,261
That's our restaurant.

374
00:23:51,763 --> 00:23:53,181
You really that excited?

375
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:57,436
Stop acting like a couple of teenagers
and get in here.

376
00:23:57,519 --> 00:23:59,312
Is she gonna come here every day?

377
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:01,064
She said she'd work the counter.

378
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:03,150
She did?

379
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:07,070
Can you call and ask
when they're installing the toilet?

380
00:24:07,154 --> 00:24:08,947
I told you, construction isn't over yet.

381
00:24:09,030 --> 00:24:12,409
What on earth did they stop for?
When are the rest of the stores moving in?

382
00:24:20,292 --> 00:24:24,296
<i>What we didn't count on</i>
<i>was an unexpected setback.</i>

383
00:24:32,053 --> 00:24:35,140
Can't you see the realtor
just dumped this on you and ran away?

384
00:24:36,391 --> 00:24:39,644
Why'd you even do this anyway?
You hate get-rich-quick schemes.

385
00:24:39,728 --> 00:24:41,980
<i>Even Steelheart</i>
<i>had entered a season</i>

386
00:24:42,063 --> 00:24:43,690
<i>when his child was reprimanding him.</i>

387
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:45,901
It would've been better
if you did nothing at all, Dad!

388
00:24:45,984 --> 00:24:48,361
You traded a valuable plot of land
for this trash!

389
00:24:48,445 --> 00:24:50,530
You said you'd never sell
the cabbage field, right?

390
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:51,490
Why did you do it?

391
00:24:51,573 --> 00:24:53,116
What about the cabbage field?

392
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:56,161
It's not a vacation house, after all.
They're building a hotel there.

393
00:24:56,244 --> 00:24:58,538
But they're building a golf course here.

394
00:24:58,622 --> 00:24:59,831
And a hospital.

395
00:24:59,915 --> 00:25:01,666
It's all a lie. All of it.

396
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,543
The realtor said that
to swindle my father!

397
00:25:06,505 --> 00:25:07,339
Look, Dad,

398
00:25:08,507 --> 00:25:11,635
the way things look to me,
you're the unluckiest guy in the world.

399
00:25:11,718 --> 00:25:12,677
Do you realize that?

400
00:25:13,428 --> 00:25:16,681
Then what happens to us?
Are they taking the apartment away?

401
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:20,977
Couldn't we pay off the interest
and list this place for sale?

402
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:24,439
Who would buy it? And how would we pay?
You wanna ask a loan shark for the money?

403
00:25:25,023 --> 00:25:26,274
All right, then.

404
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:27,943
On Monday, I'll go to the bank.

405
00:25:28,735 --> 00:25:30,278
- I'll mention I'm the owner of--
- Please!

406
00:25:30,362 --> 00:25:34,282
You know how the world works, don't you?
Banks never gamble on people like us!

407
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:37,035
If you don't know any better,
ask your children for advice!

408
00:25:37,536 --> 00:25:41,081
If you had kept that cabbage field,
we could've sent Che-il to study abroad!

409
00:25:41,581 --> 00:25:45,043
It's your father's money, understand?
It's not yours. It's your father's.

410
00:25:45,126 --> 00:25:47,337
You have no right
to raise your voice at him,

411
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:49,631
even if he was robbed.
You know why he did this?

412
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:52,092
Because you were always going,
"Money, money, money!"

413
00:25:52,175 --> 00:25:55,845
You were always pressuring him for more,
so he did this to get it for you.

414
00:25:55,929 --> 00:25:59,140
When your scheme landed you in jail,
did you discuss your plans with us?

415
00:25:59,933 --> 00:26:02,310
"If you don't know any better,
ask your children for advice."

416
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:05,146
"It would be better if you did nothing."
How dare you say that to him!

417
00:26:05,230 --> 00:26:06,439
How dare you, Eun-myeong!

418
00:26:08,858 --> 00:26:12,070
He's done everything for you.
You won't disrespect your father's life.

419
00:26:12,153 --> 00:26:13,863
He's never lived it for himself.

420
00:26:19,286 --> 00:26:21,037
Let's go home.

421
00:26:22,747 --> 00:26:24,082
I got your cash.

422
00:26:27,502 --> 00:26:30,880
<i>Goal accomplished.</i>
g.o.d.'s Babysitting Diaries.

423
00:26:32,549 --> 00:26:35,135
<i>For Jae-min to become</i>
<i>a healthier and smarter child,</i>

424
00:26:35,218 --> 00:26:38,847
<i>the big brothers of g.o.d.</i>
<i>visit a playroom with him.</i>

425
00:26:39,431 --> 00:26:41,641
<i>There's a lot for him to play with.</i>

426
00:26:41,725 --> 00:26:44,728
<i>Let's find out just how much smarter</i>
<i>Jae-min has become.</i>

427
00:26:57,073 --> 00:26:58,908
Who asked you to get us money?

428
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:04,581
Where'd you get it from?

429
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:06,916
You didn't have that many other options.

430
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:09,628
- Tell me where you got it.
- I borrowed it.

431
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:13,256
And I dipped into my savings, Mom.

432
00:27:13,882 --> 00:27:16,885
I felt humiliated asking people,
but I still did it.

433
00:27:17,594 --> 00:27:20,680
I guess you know you should be ashamed
to come to us for money.

434
00:27:20,764 --> 00:27:22,807
Why did you even come?

435
00:27:22,891 --> 00:27:26,311
Who told you to go around
asking for money? Why did you do that?

436
00:27:26,811 --> 00:27:27,771
You shouldn't have.

437
00:27:27,854 --> 00:27:31,024
How could I not?
I'm the eldest sibling, the eldest child.

438
00:27:33,610 --> 00:27:35,070
The pillar of this family.

439
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:38,239
Isn't that what you raised me to be?

440
00:27:38,323 --> 00:27:39,282
We never…

441
00:27:40,367 --> 00:27:41,409
We never meant for you to--

442
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:44,663
It's what I felt growing up,
even if it's not what you intended.

443
00:27:50,168 --> 00:27:52,087
Ever since I first started working,

444
00:27:52,587 --> 00:27:55,340
I sent you guys
a hundred thousand won each month.

445
00:27:55,423 --> 00:27:56,925
You think I wanted to send it?

446
00:27:57,008 --> 00:27:59,302
I earned that money.
Of course I wanted to keep it.

447
00:27:59,386 --> 00:28:01,304
We never asked for it.

448
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:03,723
I was always telling you
not to send it to us.

449
00:28:03,807 --> 00:28:05,684
You know why I sent that money?

450
00:28:05,767 --> 00:28:09,104
It wasn't because I was overwhelmed
with gratitude for you guys.

451
00:28:11,815 --> 00:28:13,191
It's because I felt guilty

452
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:15,652
for not wanting to send it.

453
00:28:17,028 --> 00:28:18,863
Spending it on myself felt so wrong.

454
00:28:21,324 --> 00:28:22,909
That's what family is to me.

455
00:28:24,244 --> 00:28:27,247
It's about feeling guilty over everything.
Do you know what that feels like?

456
00:28:28,206 --> 00:28:29,958
Be quiet. Your father will hear it.

457
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:33,461
If I'm this family's goddamn pillar,
why'd you send me overseas?

458
00:28:33,545 --> 00:28:36,256
Did you do all these things
just to kill me with guilt?

459
00:28:39,259 --> 00:28:41,928
I know that you guys
barely make ends meet because of me.

460
00:28:42,429 --> 00:28:45,432
All these years, you put your hopes in me
and suffered for it.

461
00:28:45,515 --> 00:28:47,100
Do you know what a burden that was?

462
00:28:47,684 --> 00:28:50,520
I'm sick of being the big fish
that made it out of the little pond!

463
00:28:50,603 --> 00:28:53,314
The pillar, the older sibling!
God, I'm sick of it all!

464
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:55,692
Yang Geum-myeong!

465
00:28:57,736 --> 00:28:59,654
<i>For the first time in my life,</i>

466
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:01,656
<i>Dad raised his voice to me.</i>

467
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:02,824
<i>"Yang Geum-myeong."</i>

468
00:29:03,491 --> 00:29:04,743
<i>That's all he said.</i>

469
00:29:07,036 --> 00:29:09,247
<i>But it stung me badly.</i>

470
00:29:09,914 --> 00:29:12,876
<i>It felt like he had told me</i>
<i>I'd never amount to anything.</i>

471
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:20,258
Goddamn brat.

472
00:29:21,676 --> 00:29:24,137
She's so arrogant. So arrogant.

473
00:29:25,096 --> 00:29:27,432
She loses her famous temper
and just leaves.

474
00:29:28,016 --> 00:29:30,685
Well, what about me? What about me?

475
00:29:31,936 --> 00:29:35,315
I've been putting up with her damn temper
ever since she was a teenager.

476
00:29:37,108 --> 00:29:39,861
She has no idea
I'm going through menopause. Jeez.

477
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:50,205
But I get how she feels.

478
00:29:51,289 --> 00:29:53,374
Being the eldest was a burden for me too.

479
00:29:54,459 --> 00:29:56,252
And now she's going through that.

480
00:29:56,336 --> 00:29:59,923
By the time you were her age,
you were already raising two children

481
00:30:00,632 --> 00:30:04,093
and had buried a third in your heart,
and all that while street vending.

482
00:30:05,053 --> 00:30:06,596
No one can do it like you.

483
00:30:07,555 --> 00:30:08,389
No one.

484
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:15,188
That stubborn girl.

485
00:30:15,772 --> 00:30:17,607
She should've taken these anyway.

486
00:30:20,819 --> 00:30:21,861
She might be stubborn,

487
00:30:22,987 --> 00:30:24,072
but she's not heartless.

488
00:30:25,156 --> 00:30:28,159
You know she's on that bus
crying her eyes out.

489
00:30:44,300 --> 00:30:46,010
<i>How could I have known then</i>

490
00:30:47,011 --> 00:30:48,638
<i>that at my mom's funeral,</i>

491
00:30:49,722 --> 00:30:52,725
<i>this day would be the first thing</i>
<i>that I'd remember?</i>

492
00:30:59,232 --> 00:31:01,317
Don't peel any more quail eggs for her.

493
00:31:01,401 --> 00:31:03,236
She doesn't seem to care anyway.

494
00:31:03,319 --> 00:31:06,281
Let's stop and rest.
You said you were having hot flashes.

495
00:31:06,364 --> 00:31:08,992
Oh, I'm so upset for some reason.

496
00:31:09,075 --> 00:31:12,370
I don't know if it's hormones or what.
I just wanna break everything.

497
00:31:26,718 --> 00:31:27,677
Oh my God.

498
00:31:28,303 --> 00:31:29,387
Oh my! Look!

499
00:31:29,470 --> 00:31:30,930
What, what? What now?

500
00:31:31,014 --> 00:31:32,348
Oh my God.

501
00:31:32,932 --> 00:31:35,101
Oh my God!

502
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:39,898
MY HORMONES ARE ALL OVER THE PLACE TOO
SORRY, GOMEN, MIAN…

503
00:31:39,981 --> 00:31:42,275
<i>It was</i>
<i>hormones versus hormones,</i>

504
00:31:42,358 --> 00:31:44,569
<i>and Mom was defeated yet again.</i>

505
00:31:44,652 --> 00:31:47,906
Why didn't she take the food?
Why didn't she?

506
00:31:49,699 --> 00:31:52,076
That's why she's been
asking around for money.

507
00:31:52,744 --> 00:31:54,579
She got pregnant, just like me.

508
00:31:57,081 --> 00:31:59,626
She feels hopeless too.

509
00:31:59,709 --> 00:32:00,793
Oh God.

510
00:32:28,363 --> 00:32:30,782
<i>Dad's world</i>
<i>was once only seven pounds.</i>

511
00:32:30,865 --> 00:32:31,741
Oh, hi.

512
00:32:31,824 --> 00:32:34,285
<i>Now,</i>
<i>she would have one of her own.</i>

513
00:32:36,245 --> 00:32:38,581
<i>Chung-seob, I can't do this.</i>

514
00:32:38,665 --> 00:32:40,750
Oh, I can't do this anymore.

515
00:32:44,337 --> 00:32:45,296
Honey?

516
00:32:46,130 --> 00:32:48,549
How bad is it?
Should I call for the doctor?

517
00:32:49,133 --> 00:32:50,301
Should I ask your mom to come?

518
00:32:52,720 --> 00:32:54,847
Can you ask the nurses again?

519
00:32:54,931 --> 00:32:57,392
Can you ask them to give me the epidural?

520
00:32:57,475 --> 00:32:59,018
Okay.

521
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:00,853
Oh, you're here.

522
00:33:03,398 --> 00:33:06,067
- Can she have the epidural?
- We cannot give her any more.

523
00:33:06,734 --> 00:33:08,486
Why not?

524
00:33:08,569 --> 00:33:11,447
You're not dilating fast enough.
The doctor ordered to stop the epidural.

525
00:33:11,531 --> 00:33:14,283
Wait, wait, hold on.
That doesn't make any sense?

526
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:16,411
She's had contractions the past 12 hours.

527
00:33:16,995 --> 00:33:18,871
My… my wife is very weak.

528
00:33:19,539 --> 00:33:23,584
The real problem
is that… the baby won't move.

529
00:33:24,919 --> 00:33:26,879
Mr. Park, you need to sign a waiver form.

530
00:33:26,963 --> 00:33:29,257
- In the event the mother and child…
- My wife.

531
00:33:29,799 --> 00:33:30,633
Save her.

532
00:33:32,218 --> 00:33:33,594
No matter what, save her.

533
00:33:34,554 --> 00:33:36,514
Wait, but why?

534
00:33:36,597 --> 00:33:38,182
Why isn't it moving?

535
00:33:50,486 --> 00:33:52,280
Hello, Mother. Hi.

536
00:33:53,573 --> 00:33:56,576
The thing is, I'm not sure
what's going on right now.

537
00:33:56,659 --> 00:33:58,077
She's fully dilated,

538
00:33:59,495 --> 00:34:01,831
but the baby doesn't wanna come out.

539
00:34:04,625 --> 00:34:06,502
They say it's obstructed labor.

540
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:07,420
<i>Honestly…</i>

541
00:34:09,630 --> 00:34:10,631
they're not doing well.

542
00:34:10,715 --> 00:34:13,301
Uh… uh, what's the problem? What's wrong?

543
00:34:13,885 --> 00:34:16,220
<i>Uh, is… is… is she in danger?</i>

544
00:34:16,304 --> 00:34:17,472
<i>Is something wrong?</i>

545
00:34:18,181 --> 00:34:19,766
Mother, I'm sorry to ask,

546
00:34:20,349 --> 00:34:21,642
but could you come over?

547
00:34:22,643 --> 00:34:24,103
Geum-myeong's asking for you.

548
00:34:24,937 --> 00:34:26,314
She's asking for her mom.

549
00:34:29,275 --> 00:34:31,110
Sweetie, what is it? What's wrong?

550
00:34:31,194 --> 00:34:33,738
<i>As the young branch</i>
<i>was developing a new shoot…</i>

551
00:34:33,821 --> 00:34:34,655
<i>Hang on.</i>

552
00:34:34,739 --> 00:34:38,284
<i>…the whole tree shook with fear</i>
<i>and grew tense.</i>

553
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:40,620
One, two, three.

554
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:42,371
No, not yet, not yet.

555
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:45,333
Now push. Push, push, push.

556
00:34:46,125 --> 00:34:48,836
One, two, three, four.

557
00:34:50,046 --> 00:34:53,091
No, don't stop now.
That would be very bad.

558
00:34:53,174 --> 00:34:54,759
But it hurts so much.

559
00:34:54,842 --> 00:34:58,679
Okay, breathe, breathe.
Push, push, push, push.

560
00:34:58,763 --> 00:35:01,724
One, two, three, four.

561
00:35:02,558 --> 00:35:05,353
- Come on, you have to push.
- I think I'm about to pass out.

562
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:09,565
Again, one, two, three.

563
00:35:09,649 --> 00:35:11,150
Keep breathing. Don't stop.

564
00:35:11,234 --> 00:35:13,611
I need you to push a little more.
Push, push, push.

565
00:35:13,694 --> 00:35:16,864
One, two. Don't stop now. Don't stop!

566
00:35:16,948 --> 00:35:19,367
Come on. Wake up. Wake up!

567
00:35:19,992 --> 00:35:22,537
Oh no, no, no, no.
Mom, you can't give up now.

568
00:35:22,620 --> 00:35:25,790
Mom, Mom, don't stop now.
Your baby is in danger.

569
00:35:25,873 --> 00:35:27,250
She's stuck at the shoulders.

570
00:35:27,333 --> 00:35:29,585
Mom, don't you wanna see your baby?

571
00:35:29,669 --> 00:35:31,212
Don't you wanna see your baby?

572
00:35:35,591 --> 00:35:37,760
Geum-myeong,
you follow your grandma, okay?

573
00:35:37,844 --> 00:35:41,430
Go to her place and get something to eat.
I'll see you soon, okay, dear?

574
00:35:41,514 --> 00:35:44,475
It's all right. It's all right.
Don't worry, cutie, okay? Okay?

575
00:35:54,485 --> 00:35:57,363
She's alive.
Hurry, get the baby to cry.

576
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:11,460
<i>We made two resolutions.</i>

577
00:36:12,378 --> 00:36:14,380
<i>The first was to treat Mom well,</i>

578
00:36:14,881 --> 00:36:15,882
<i>and the second…</i>

579
00:36:15,965 --> 00:36:17,425
We're not having another one.

580
00:36:18,593 --> 00:36:21,220
We're not. We're not having another one.

581
00:36:21,762 --> 00:36:23,181
Stop making me laugh.

582
00:36:23,264 --> 00:36:25,057
<i>The government has paid off</i>
<i>the emergency funds</i>

583
00:36:25,141 --> 00:36:26,267
<i>loaned to it by the IMF,</i>

584
00:36:26,350 --> 00:36:28,978
<i>and Korea is now</i>
<i>back in control of its economy.</i>

585
00:36:29,061 --> 00:36:30,396
<i>Due to the risk of a national…</i>

586
00:36:30,479 --> 00:36:33,816
I guess Sae-bom is
a financial crisis baby, isn't she, huh?

587
00:36:34,483 --> 00:36:37,320
You and I met inside the theater
at the start of the crisis,

588
00:36:37,820 --> 00:36:39,947
and she was born on the day that it ended.

589
00:36:40,740 --> 00:36:42,950
Really. Some coincidence, huh?

590
00:36:44,076 --> 00:36:44,952
Right?

591
00:36:50,374 --> 00:36:52,627
What is it? Should I call the doctor?

592
00:36:53,377 --> 00:36:55,213
Are you in pain? What's wrong?

593
00:36:56,589 --> 00:36:57,506
I just…

594
00:36:58,507 --> 00:37:00,927
I just can't believe it really happened.

595
00:37:01,010 --> 00:37:02,303
I mean, how?

596
00:37:02,887 --> 00:37:05,223
I know. They made you suffer for 28 hours.

597
00:37:05,306 --> 00:37:08,184
It's outrageous!
That much pain would kill a cow!

598
00:37:08,267 --> 00:37:13,064
Yeah, but how did my mom have me
when she was 18 years old?

599
00:37:13,147 --> 00:37:15,107
She was only a child.

600
00:37:15,191 --> 00:37:17,944
<i>In the blink of an eye,</i>
<i>my mom had become a mother-in-law</i>

601
00:37:18,027 --> 00:37:19,153
<i>and a grandma.</i>

602
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:22,156
<i>Our lives had gone through</i>
<i>so many changes so quickly,</i>

603
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,658
<i>it was overwhelming.</i>

604
00:37:23,741 --> 00:37:24,909
When I think of how

605
00:37:25,493 --> 00:37:27,453
her own mother had already passed,

606
00:37:28,079 --> 00:37:30,081
of how there was no epidural.

607
00:37:30,915 --> 00:37:33,167
Just think of what she had gone through.

608
00:37:33,918 --> 00:37:35,127
And that's not it.

609
00:37:35,628 --> 00:37:38,798
When my brother was born,
she had to ride in a rickety carriage.

610
00:37:44,470 --> 00:37:45,805
Honey!

611
00:37:46,597 --> 00:37:47,723
Mom.

612
00:37:47,807 --> 00:37:48,891
Mommy's here.

613
00:37:50,726 --> 00:37:51,894
Oh, Mom.

614
00:37:52,770 --> 00:37:53,729
Good job, honey.

615
00:37:53,813 --> 00:37:56,565
<i>Their little baby</i>
<i>now had a baby of her own.</i>

616
00:37:56,649 --> 00:37:57,483
So proud.

617
00:37:57,566 --> 00:38:00,152
<i>The moment</i>
<i>they stepped into that room,</i>

618
00:38:00,653 --> 00:38:04,657
<i>they became my fortress,</i>
<i>and I was their little girl once again.</i>

619
00:38:11,872 --> 00:38:13,207
Uh, hi, Father.

620
00:38:15,209 --> 00:38:18,629
Uh… you know, Father, I sometimes think

621
00:38:19,588 --> 00:38:22,675
that it feels like I married
the princess of Tangerine Island.

622
00:38:23,259 --> 00:38:24,552
Is that a complaint?

623
00:38:24,635 --> 00:38:25,845
Sae-bom is well.

624
00:38:25,928 --> 00:38:30,349
Take this. It's seaweed soup
with sea urchins. Real ones.

625
00:38:30,433 --> 00:38:31,726
The aunties harvested them.

626
00:38:31,809 --> 00:38:34,103
I'm curious.
Who do you think Sae-bom looks like?

627
00:38:34,186 --> 00:38:37,523
My mom and her sisters
all think she has Geum-myeong's nose.

628
00:38:38,482 --> 00:38:39,442
She has her nose, eh?

629
00:38:39,525 --> 00:38:41,485
- She does?
- Oh, you haven't seen her?

630
00:38:41,569 --> 00:38:43,821
- I'm sure they'd let you…
- We will. Don't worry.

631
00:38:47,116 --> 00:38:50,244
Did you assume we'd go
to your daughter before our own?

632
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:52,079
I mean the world to my parents.

633
00:38:52,621 --> 00:38:54,874
- Just keep that in mind going forward.
- Okay.

634
00:38:55,958 --> 00:38:59,003
What did the doctor say?
She's all right, isn't she?

635
00:38:59,086 --> 00:39:01,255
Yes, she's a big girl.
Already eight pounds.

636
00:39:01,339 --> 00:39:03,341
They X-rayed her shoulders,
and everything's fine.

637
00:39:03,424 --> 00:39:05,051
Not her. I meant Geum-myeong.

638
00:39:06,052 --> 00:39:08,763
Is her gestational diabetes
over now that she's given birth?

639
00:39:08,846 --> 00:39:09,680
Oh, yes.

640
00:39:10,306 --> 00:39:13,142
I assure you,
your daughter is perfectly healthy.

641
00:39:13,642 --> 00:39:16,729
Are you trying to pick a fight with me,
or does it just feel that way?

642
00:39:17,229 --> 00:39:19,774
<i>Every time</i>
<i>I visited my parents, they had chicken</i>

643
00:39:19,857 --> 00:39:21,192
<i>and gave me the drumsticks.</i>

644
00:39:21,275 --> 00:39:22,777
<i>I was always their number one.</i>

645
00:39:22,860 --> 00:39:25,363
Oh, you already
bought baby clothes?

646
00:39:26,572 --> 00:39:29,533
They're all the best quality.
Dad didn't even look at the price.

647
00:39:29,617 --> 00:39:31,911
He just asked for the most expensive ones.

648
00:39:31,994 --> 00:39:34,747
Wha-- Why does a newborn
need expensive clothes?

649
00:39:35,289 --> 00:39:38,125
Your dad
has a new dream for himself.

650
00:39:39,085 --> 00:39:40,836
To be the rich grandpa for once.

651
00:39:41,379 --> 00:39:43,172
Jesus, I didn't mean that, Dad.

652
00:39:43,255 --> 00:39:45,508
Why do you have to take everything I say
to heart?

653
00:39:45,591 --> 00:39:46,592
Here.

654
00:39:47,468 --> 00:39:48,636
Why don't we go see

655
00:39:49,428 --> 00:39:50,805
if Sae-bom has her nose or not?

656
00:39:50,888 --> 00:39:54,517
<i>With Sae-bom's birth,</i>
<i>springtime had arrived yet again.</i>

657
00:39:57,103 --> 00:39:59,647
REALTOR HAN MAN-CHEOL!
YOUR FAMILY WILL BE CURSED!

658
00:39:59,730 --> 00:40:02,274
WHY ABANDON THESE BUILDINGS?
OWN UP TO PEOPLE'S MONEY!

659
00:40:08,989 --> 00:40:11,909
JEJU'S JANUARY DAYTIME TEMPERATURE
REACHES 21.4 DEGREES CELSIUS

660
00:40:13,285 --> 00:40:15,413
<i>And, like so many times before,</i>

661
00:40:15,913 --> 00:40:19,125
<i>my parents survived</i>
<i>yet another winter together.</i>

662
00:40:36,142 --> 00:40:38,352
You really wanna run this restaurant?

663
00:40:38,436 --> 00:40:40,271
You think people will like it?

664
00:40:40,896 --> 00:40:43,441
They'll just have to take
a five-minute detour.

665
00:40:43,524 --> 00:40:45,734
They can sit down, eat quickly, and go.

666
00:40:45,818 --> 00:40:47,611
We'll give them plenty
to justify the trip.

667
00:40:48,779 --> 00:40:50,072
But will they take that trip?

668
00:40:50,156 --> 00:40:53,617
Hell, if they don't come to us…
we'll take it to them.

669
00:40:54,827 --> 00:40:56,662
You wanna do delivery?

670
00:40:58,372 --> 00:41:00,749
<i>Jjajangmyeon </i>can be delivered, but squids…

671
00:41:02,209 --> 00:41:04,170
I caught squids for over 30 years.

672
00:41:04,253 --> 00:41:06,464
There's nothing you can't do with squids.

673
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:09,508
They don't know anything out here.

674
00:41:09,592 --> 00:41:12,136
Here, they overcharge you
for a dead squid.

675
00:41:12,219 --> 00:41:14,430
We're going to give them
the freshest squids you can get.

676
00:41:14,513 --> 00:41:16,474
It'll be the tastiest and the cheapest

677
00:41:16,557 --> 00:41:18,476
and will be delivered the fastest.

678
00:41:18,559 --> 00:41:19,560
It's a no-brainer.

679
00:41:25,858 --> 00:41:26,817
And besides,

680
00:41:28,152 --> 00:41:29,570
we've worked hard before.

681
00:41:30,488 --> 00:41:31,947
We can work hard again.

682
00:41:33,699 --> 00:41:34,575
My love,

683
00:41:35,868 --> 00:41:36,994
you know me.

684
00:41:40,539 --> 00:41:43,959
You know, if we do this,
I'll give it my all.

685
00:41:47,546 --> 00:41:48,631
I know you will.

686
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:53,928
We'll do this the only way we know how.

687
00:42:02,311 --> 00:42:05,189
<i>And so,</i>
<i>they resolved to do what they did best.</i>

688
00:42:05,272 --> 00:42:09,276
<i>It was the same mentality that once</i>
<i>helped Mom plow that stony field</i>

689
00:42:09,360 --> 00:42:11,820
<i>and Dad sail into the deepest seas.</i>

690
00:42:45,688 --> 00:42:46,689
Hello.

691
00:42:56,282 --> 00:42:59,326
GEUMEUNDONG'S
WE AIM TO GET IT DONE IN 10 MINUTES!

692
00:43:04,456 --> 00:43:06,667
<i>The heavens</i>
<i>must have taken pity on us</i>

693
00:43:06,750 --> 00:43:08,752
<i>because, like</i>
<i>the Korean national soccer team,</i>

694
00:43:09,336 --> 00:43:11,130
<i>we kept getting corner kicks.</i>

695
00:43:11,213 --> 00:43:12,715
<i>Soccer games meant deliveries.</i>

696
00:43:13,549 --> 00:43:15,926
<i>- And soon, it was 2002.</i>
- <i>He shoots, he scores!</i>

697
00:43:16,010 --> 00:43:18,178
<i>Park Ji-sung! He scores!</i>

698
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:20,306
<i>Park Ji-sung!</i>

699
00:43:20,389 --> 00:43:22,725
<i>- South Korea is ahead of Portugal!</i>
- Did we score?

700
00:43:22,808 --> 00:43:24,560
- Incredible!
<i>- One to zero!</i>

701
00:43:28,188 --> 00:43:29,773
Hey, Gwan-sik!

702
00:43:32,693 --> 00:43:34,570
I told you Park Ji-sung would score!

703
00:43:34,653 --> 00:43:35,904
Park Ji-sung!

704
00:43:35,988 --> 00:43:37,865
I've been waiting 20 years for this!

705
00:43:37,948 --> 00:43:39,366
Hey, hey, hey. What is that?

706
00:43:39,450 --> 00:43:41,493
Bring me a box of raw squid! A whole box!

707
00:43:41,577 --> 00:43:44,413
Oh, oh, oh! Yeah!

708
00:43:45,164 --> 00:43:46,332
<i>Daehanminguk!</i>

709
00:43:46,415 --> 00:43:48,751
<i>Their business tactics</i>
<i>would be similar.</i>

710
00:43:48,834 --> 00:43:52,755
<i>Dad would be Park Ji-sung,</i>
<i>and Mom would be Coach Hiddink.</i>

711
00:43:53,422 --> 00:43:54,506
Let's be honest here.

712
00:43:54,590 --> 00:43:57,301
No one in Jeju knows squid
better than we do.

713
00:43:57,926 --> 00:44:00,179
Certainly not those mainland amateurs.

714
00:44:00,262 --> 00:44:02,514
They may run your restaurants,
but they're phoning it in.

715
00:44:02,598 --> 00:44:03,682
You know they'll all fail.

716
00:44:03,766 --> 00:44:06,352
They think squids are nothing
but side dishes!

717
00:44:06,435 --> 00:44:09,813
It's an afterthought. Take it or leave it.
But for us, squid is the star!

718
00:44:09,897 --> 00:44:12,024
To us, the squid is Ahn Jung-hwan.

719
00:44:13,025 --> 00:44:14,526
Oh boy.

720
00:44:14,610 --> 00:44:16,612
- So that's Gwan-sik's wife?
- Uh-huh.

721
00:44:16,695 --> 00:44:19,031
How about it, Captain?
Give us an exclusive.

722
00:44:20,157 --> 00:44:21,075
It's an easy call.

723
00:44:21,158 --> 00:44:22,910
So what about it?

724
00:44:22,993 --> 00:44:25,120
You haven't mentioned
how much you're willing to pay.

725
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:26,914
Well, we can't pay you too much right now.

726
00:44:26,997 --> 00:44:27,956
Yeesh.

727
00:44:28,916 --> 00:44:31,043
Soon, you'll be asking us
to take your squids,

728
00:44:31,126 --> 00:44:32,127
but it'll be too late.

729
00:44:32,211 --> 00:44:33,587
It's now or never.

730
00:44:33,671 --> 00:44:36,423
She's a stubborn one, isn't she?

731
00:44:37,091 --> 00:44:38,926
You think she gets her way with Gwan-sik?

732
00:44:39,009 --> 00:44:41,095
Do you have to ask? It's obvious.

733
00:44:41,178 --> 00:44:44,056
And why am I having this conversation
with you instead of Gwan-sik?

734
00:44:44,765 --> 00:44:48,227
That's how it's always been.
The women call the shots in that family.

735
00:44:49,687 --> 00:44:50,854
GEUMEUNDONG'S
CEO, OH AE-SUN

736
00:44:50,938 --> 00:44:54,233
I need a yes or a no.
Don't give me a maybe.

737
00:44:56,235 --> 00:44:58,070
The decision
to buy Samsung stocks

738
00:44:58,153 --> 00:45:00,322
worth 300 won or three million…

739
00:45:02,366 --> 00:45:04,368
that is entirely up to you.

740
00:45:07,830 --> 00:45:09,248
To be honest, sir,

741
00:45:10,332 --> 00:45:13,043
I'm meeting with
two more people after you.

742
00:45:13,877 --> 00:45:16,296
I'm ready to make you an industry leader,

743
00:45:16,380 --> 00:45:19,216
but if you choose
not to go on this journey together,

744
00:45:20,008 --> 00:45:21,844
I'll have to find
the next diamond in the rough.

745
00:45:23,721 --> 00:45:24,972
This may be your last chance.

746
00:45:25,556 --> 00:45:26,515
Well…

747
00:45:27,141 --> 00:45:29,643
It goes to show
how much I believe in this idea.

748
00:45:29,727 --> 00:45:33,105
This won't just change the industry.
It'll redefine it.

749
00:45:33,188 --> 00:45:36,108
And what's the story
with your company's name?

750
00:45:37,109 --> 00:45:39,069
Ah, it comes from my mother.

751
00:45:41,655 --> 00:45:44,199
Growing up, this was always her motto.

752
00:45:53,167 --> 00:45:56,754
"Domestic duty-free stores
to open in Jeju."

753
00:45:57,296 --> 00:46:00,466
Does that mean Koreans
can buy cigarettes tax-free there?

754
00:46:01,341 --> 00:46:03,719
- That a question for your father-in-law?
- Honey.

755
00:46:04,511 --> 00:46:07,181
My friends keep asking me
to buy them a big bundle of cigarettes

756
00:46:07,264 --> 00:46:08,640
every time I go to Seoul.

757
00:46:08,724 --> 00:46:11,977
I guess they think that you can buy
anything at the duty-free store.

758
00:46:12,561 --> 00:46:14,146
Your friends are morons.

759
00:46:15,481 --> 00:46:18,650
I never thought something
the government did would actually help us.

760
00:46:18,734 --> 00:46:21,737
If we get more tourists,
people are going to order our food

761
00:46:21,820 --> 00:46:23,405
from the resorts up the mountain.

762
00:46:23,489 --> 00:46:25,949
Has that film crew
not called us from their motel?

763
00:46:26,700 --> 00:46:28,619
Are they ordering from somewhere else?

764
00:46:28,702 --> 00:46:31,872
Oh yeah.
What are they filming in Jeju anyway?

765
00:46:31,955 --> 00:46:34,541
It's for a film starring… What's his name?

766
00:46:35,083 --> 00:46:36,710
The guy with the nice teeth. Um…

767
00:46:40,172 --> 00:46:42,216
Oh, Lee Byung-hun. Lee Byung-hun.

768
00:46:42,299 --> 00:46:44,593
Ah, Lee Byung-hun.

769
00:46:44,676 --> 00:46:47,763
UNLIMITED REFILLS OF SQUID SOUP
FOR DINE-IN CUSTOMERS

770
00:46:47,846 --> 00:46:50,766
{\an8}<i>The free kicks didn't stop.</i>

771
00:46:50,849 --> 00:46:52,017
Yes.

772
00:46:52,100 --> 00:46:54,478
If you dine in
instead of ordering delivery,

773
00:46:54,561 --> 00:46:56,688
you'll be given a 10% discount.

774
00:46:57,564 --> 00:46:58,524
Yes.

775
00:46:58,607 --> 00:47:00,442
That's right, 10%.

776
00:47:00,526 --> 00:47:01,819
Hello. Welcome!

777
00:47:01,902 --> 00:47:05,072
This must be Byun-sama's
favorite spot. Look, his autograph.

778
00:47:05,155 --> 00:47:07,407
Oh, so is his picture.

779
00:47:07,491 --> 00:47:09,409
Jeez, another pair of <i>arigatous.</i>

780
00:47:09,493 --> 00:47:11,703
Wait a minute. Wait a minute, please.

781
00:47:11,787 --> 00:47:13,413
I wonder where he sat.

782
00:47:14,039 --> 00:47:15,582
- Right here.
- Right here?

783
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:17,334
Oh, Mother?

784
00:47:17,417 --> 00:47:20,671
They're selling restaurant chairs
on Joonggonara. Should we get some?

785
00:47:20,754 --> 00:47:22,047
Wait. Here you go.

786
00:47:22,548 --> 00:47:24,383
You think we need them?

787
00:47:24,466 --> 00:47:26,677
<i>That was when</i>
<i>Joonggonara was brand new.</i>

788
00:47:26,760 --> 00:47:27,594
Hey!

789
00:47:28,887 --> 00:47:29,721
Hey!

790
00:47:30,222 --> 00:47:31,181
Get the family together!

791
00:47:31,265 --> 00:47:33,392
What?
We're family all of a sudden?

792
00:47:33,475 --> 00:47:35,602
You were supposed to be watching the kids.

793
00:47:35,686 --> 00:47:38,730
<i>Thanks to Joonggonara,</i>
<i>we heard a name we'd given up on.</i>

794
00:47:38,814 --> 00:47:39,648
Cheol-yong.

795
00:47:42,109 --> 00:47:43,527
Cheol-yong, I said!

796
00:47:44,444 --> 00:47:46,405
Park Cheol-yong's arrested by the cops!

797
00:47:46,488 --> 00:47:47,656
Oh my God!

798
00:47:48,156 --> 00:47:50,158
They found the <i>buncheong </i>stoneware!

799
00:47:53,412 --> 00:47:56,123
I guess nobody wanted
to pay him the 70 million.

800
00:47:56,206 --> 00:47:57,624
He couldn't get rid of it,

801
00:47:57,708 --> 00:48:01,420
so that moron
put the whole set up online for sale.

802
00:48:03,213 --> 00:48:05,257
So then, um, we're keeping the stoneware?

803
00:48:05,340 --> 00:48:06,300
Huh.

804
00:48:08,677 --> 00:48:09,511
Yes?

805
00:48:10,095 --> 00:48:10,971
Yes?

806
00:48:11,471 --> 00:48:12,514
Who's speaking?

807
00:48:13,807 --> 00:48:15,267
<i>Direct penalty kick.</i>

808
00:48:15,350 --> 00:48:16,435
Come again?

809
00:48:24,401 --> 00:48:26,194
<i>It was yet another season</i>

810
00:48:26,278 --> 00:48:29,239
<i>when past kindness begat another kindness.</i>

811
00:48:32,117 --> 00:48:33,744
She's as pure as a white dove.

812
00:48:44,838 --> 00:48:47,841
Mmm. This taste
is what I come to Jeju for.

813
00:48:48,926 --> 00:48:51,762
The squid soup here
is my ultimate comfort food.

814
00:48:52,429 --> 00:48:53,555
You could say

815
00:48:54,306 --> 00:48:55,349
it saved my life.

816
00:49:01,563 --> 00:49:03,941
- Is she a regular?
- Never seen her.

817
00:49:04,024 --> 00:49:08,320
Uh, Miss Jeong, um,
could you say that famous phrase?

818
00:49:08,403 --> 00:49:10,864
Excuse me. We agreed
you wouldn't make her say that.

819
00:49:10,948 --> 00:49:12,950
Just one shot of her saying it.

820
00:49:14,242 --> 00:49:16,703
It's all right. I'll give it a shot.

821
00:49:19,998 --> 00:49:22,918
"Squid soup for sale. Soup!"

822
00:49:23,418 --> 00:49:24,252
How was that?

823
00:49:28,966 --> 00:49:30,550
Just like in the movie!

824
00:49:37,182 --> 00:49:39,184
{\an8}SOUP FOR SALE, SOUP!
GEUMEUNDONG'S SQUID SOUP

825
00:49:39,267 --> 00:49:40,978
{\an8}I CAN VOUCH FOR THIS PLACE
JEONG MI-IN

826
00:49:51,113 --> 00:49:54,533
You must really love squid.
I've never seen you eat like that before.

827
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:57,619
- I don't eat seafood.
- What?

828
00:49:57,703 --> 00:50:00,998
Go have a smoke and get directions
to our next location.

829
00:50:01,999 --> 00:50:02,833
Fine.

830
00:50:08,338 --> 00:50:11,967
Miss Jeong, you know you can trust me,
so be honest with me here.

831
00:50:12,050 --> 00:50:14,761
I don't care if you went to Macau,
and you got your face done.

832
00:50:14,845 --> 00:50:16,930
I need you to always tell me the truth.

833
00:50:19,099 --> 00:50:22,185
Is it… something to do with that man?

834
00:50:22,811 --> 00:50:25,689
There's nothing between you,
is there? Hmm?

835
00:50:25,772 --> 00:50:27,065
- Hey.
- Is there?

836
00:50:27,149 --> 00:50:29,401
Would I be here if there were nothing?

837
00:50:29,484 --> 00:50:31,319
Don't do this to me, Miss Jeong.

838
00:50:31,403 --> 00:50:33,905
I have to send child support in dollars.

839
00:50:36,241 --> 00:50:38,201
That man is the reason
you can pay your bills.

840
00:50:38,785 --> 00:50:41,705
He's the only reason
that Rolex is on your wrist right now.

841
00:50:47,127 --> 00:50:49,921
<i>When the scandal blew up in my face,</i>
<i>I wanted to die.</i>

842
00:50:52,299 --> 00:50:54,176
<i>If I died from carbon monoxide,</i>

843
00:50:54,259 --> 00:50:55,886
<i>there'd be pictures of me.</i>

844
00:50:55,969 --> 00:50:59,181
<i>If I fell off a high place,</i>
<i>I would become a spectacle.</i>

845
00:51:04,853 --> 00:51:08,065
<i>So… I got on a fishing boat.</i>

846
00:51:09,858 --> 00:51:11,359
All right.

847
00:51:25,415 --> 00:51:28,418
<i>Woo-ryeong once told me</i>
<i>that she wanted to hang herself one night,</i>

848
00:51:28,502 --> 00:51:30,504
<i>but she started to shave her legs first.</i>

849
00:51:31,254 --> 00:51:33,882
<i>While shaving,</i>
<i>she realized how idiotic it all was,</i>

850
00:51:33,965 --> 00:51:35,425
<i>so she changed her mind.</i>

851
00:51:36,718 --> 00:51:39,054
<i>Not even a dog would wanna live my life.</i>

852
00:51:39,554 --> 00:51:41,807
<i>I had no more desire to live.</i>

853
00:51:44,226 --> 00:51:45,685
But that man saved me.

854
00:51:47,479 --> 00:51:49,189
I was a complete wreck.

855
00:51:49,773 --> 00:51:52,651
I heard people's voices
and the ambulance on its way.

856
00:51:53,235 --> 00:51:56,696
Even at that point,
all I wanted was to cover my face.

857
00:51:59,407 --> 00:52:00,826
And that man there

858
00:52:02,327 --> 00:52:05,080
took off his jacket and covered it for me.

859
00:52:07,791 --> 00:52:09,334
For the first time in my life,

860
00:52:09,876 --> 00:52:12,796
while everyone else wanted
to reveal my shame,

861
00:52:13,296 --> 00:52:14,673
that man covered it.

862
00:52:15,590 --> 00:52:16,591
PIECE OF JUNK

863
00:52:16,675 --> 00:52:19,094
All right.
This banana milk is nothing.

864
00:52:19,177 --> 00:52:20,053
That bigwig…

865
00:52:20,137 --> 00:52:21,680
<i>I went back to see him once</i>

866
00:52:21,763 --> 00:52:23,640
<i>because I couldn't forget</i>
<i>what he did for me.</i>

867
00:52:24,641 --> 00:52:25,559
Oh God.

868
00:52:25,642 --> 00:52:28,770
It makes no difference if he's buying pork
if it's a secret ballot.

869
00:52:29,271 --> 00:52:31,648
People eat and still vote how they want.

870
00:52:31,731 --> 00:52:33,441
I'm sure they'll want Ae-sun.

871
00:52:34,901 --> 00:52:37,612
<i>He lived as a man should.</i>
<i>Exactly as he should.</i>

872
00:53:00,177 --> 00:53:02,512
So, don't you not recognize me?

873
00:53:02,596 --> 00:53:05,473
I won an award
for supporting actress yesterday.

874
00:53:05,557 --> 00:53:07,058
I played a fisherman's wife.

875
00:53:10,270 --> 00:53:11,938
I'm doing much better these days.

876
00:53:12,731 --> 00:53:14,941
I thought there might be
some way to repay you.

877
00:53:15,025 --> 00:53:16,610
Oh, no. It was nothing.

878
00:53:17,235 --> 00:53:18,612
I couldn't accept a thing.

879
00:53:20,155 --> 00:53:21,740
It was true then, and it's true now.

880
00:53:23,658 --> 00:53:25,577
I can breathe again, thanks to you.

881
00:53:26,286 --> 00:53:29,206
I want you to know
that nothing would make me happier

882
00:53:29,289 --> 00:53:31,291
than the chance to repay you for that.

883
00:53:32,083 --> 00:53:34,252
If there's anything, please let me know.

884
00:53:39,257 --> 00:53:40,759
There's a lot I can do.

885
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:45,138
<i>Who needs luck</i>
<i>when you have kindness?</i>

886
00:53:45,222 --> 00:53:47,891
<i>It was only a reward</i>
<i>for the man with a heart of gold.</i>

887
00:53:47,974 --> 00:53:50,352
What if that man fights
with his wife over this?

888
00:53:50,435 --> 00:53:52,187
She's bound to suspect something.

889
00:53:52,270 --> 00:53:54,439
Why would you appear
at their restaurant out of the blue?

890
00:53:54,522 --> 00:53:57,359
- She might know about it.
- I don't think she does.

891
00:53:57,442 --> 00:54:00,528
Usually, men keep
that sort of thing to themselves.

892
00:54:00,612 --> 00:54:02,364
It avoids conflict with the wife.

893
00:54:02,447 --> 00:54:04,074
Well, you know what they say.

894
00:54:04,157 --> 00:54:07,577
The way a man acts in life
is how he's remembered after he's gone.

895
00:54:09,037 --> 00:54:11,164
Why did you look at me when you said that?

896
00:54:17,170 --> 00:54:19,214
See? I told you she would come.

897
00:54:19,297 --> 00:54:21,716
She came back a few years ago to thank me.

898
00:54:22,968 --> 00:54:24,970
You must have said that a hundred times.

899
00:54:25,053 --> 00:54:27,013
You just wanna show off, don't you?

900
00:54:27,097 --> 00:54:30,016
Well, yeah, I saved a star.

901
00:54:30,100 --> 00:54:32,435
I mean,
this is sort of impressive, isn't it?

902
00:54:39,025 --> 00:54:41,152
You see how dirty Sang-gil is looking?

903
00:54:41,778 --> 00:54:43,989
Just look at his shirt collar.
It's filthy.

904
00:54:44,739 --> 00:54:47,367
You reap what you sow in life, don't you?

905
00:54:47,450 --> 00:54:50,578
One man has faced down
all manner of storms and never budged.

906
00:54:50,662 --> 00:54:53,456
Meanwhile, the other man
has spread himself thin all over town.

907
00:54:53,540 --> 00:54:56,668
How can you compare them?
They're completely different animals.

908
00:55:01,339 --> 00:55:05,051
THE SHARE OF SO-CALLED "GRAY DIVORCES"
INCREASED BY 18%

909
00:55:08,972 --> 00:55:10,140
Those shoes are really nice.

910
00:55:11,099 --> 00:55:12,058
They're very light.

911
00:55:12,726 --> 00:55:14,436
The Maasai tribe wears them, apparently.

912
00:55:29,868 --> 00:55:31,161
Where did you get these?

913
00:55:31,244 --> 00:55:33,830
I have no idea.
I just wear what they buy me.

914
00:55:36,041 --> 00:55:38,710
- They buy you shoes?
- Yeah, my wife and kids get them.

915
00:55:53,725 --> 00:55:55,852
Come. You should eat before you go.

916
00:55:55,935 --> 00:55:57,937
I could just eat at home, you know.

917
00:55:58,021 --> 00:56:00,357
But why would you eat alone?
Just eat here.

918
00:56:00,440 --> 00:56:02,275
My goodness, look at your belly!

919
00:56:02,359 --> 00:56:04,527
That's what nothing
but <i>ramyeon </i>will do to you.

920
00:56:07,155 --> 00:56:09,449
And for the love of God, get a haircut!

921
00:56:09,532 --> 00:56:11,368
Are you avoiding it
because you're going bald?

922
00:56:12,827 --> 00:56:16,373
Well, all right.
Thanks for inviting me.

923
00:56:17,707 --> 00:56:18,541
<i>Arigatou.</i>

924
00:56:18,625 --> 00:56:21,044
Hey, why can't you thank them
like a normal person?

925
00:56:21,127 --> 00:56:24,255
Were you not planning
on fulfilling your duties as a father?

926
00:56:27,842 --> 00:56:29,469
Just eat here, Dad.

927
00:56:36,601 --> 00:56:39,354
{\an8}BRIDE BU JEONG-SUK
DAUGHTER OF BU SANG-GIL AND PARK YEONG-RAN

928
00:56:40,563 --> 00:56:42,399
You don't have to be so harsh.

929
00:56:42,482 --> 00:56:44,692
It's not like he let us down in every way.

930
00:56:44,776 --> 00:56:45,610
Right.

931
00:56:45,693 --> 00:56:47,654
He did provide for you all, I suppose.

932
00:56:48,154 --> 00:56:49,447
I meant the Cheol-yong thing.

933
00:56:51,074 --> 00:56:52,951
You know Dad's the one who got him caught?

934
00:56:54,577 --> 00:56:56,955
You pierce your child's heart
with a dagger.

935
00:56:57,038 --> 00:56:59,124
No amount of money can pull it out.

936
00:56:59,207 --> 00:57:01,584
You think you're the only one who cares?

937
00:57:02,335 --> 00:57:03,545
I care a lot too.

938
00:57:04,254 --> 00:57:06,714
I care more than you do.

939
00:57:07,298 --> 00:57:09,175
Of course you work hard.

940
00:57:09,259 --> 00:57:13,972
However, you have to choose
which cases you prioritize, don't you?

941
00:57:15,098 --> 00:57:17,934
Can't you give me something more here?
You're the lead detective.

942
00:57:18,017 --> 00:57:20,770
Money can make this go away, no?
Why doesn't he settle?

943
00:57:21,980 --> 00:57:23,940
If he does that,
it's as good as pleading guilty.

944
00:57:24,023 --> 00:57:26,651
If he really stole the thing,
he should face the consequences.

945
00:57:26,734 --> 00:57:28,319
But why should a victim pay?

946
00:57:28,403 --> 00:57:30,572
Besides, even if he settled
for such and such amount,

947
00:57:31,072 --> 00:57:33,283
everyone will always
talk about him like a criminal.

948
00:57:33,366 --> 00:57:36,369
Well, well, well.
You do care about your son-in-law.

949
00:57:36,453 --> 00:57:37,871
I thought you couldn't stand him.

950
00:57:37,954 --> 00:57:39,581
That's why I know he's innocent.

951
00:57:40,165 --> 00:57:41,583
Eun-myeong's weak.

952
00:57:41,666 --> 00:57:44,085
He doesn't have
what it takes to see it through.

953
00:57:44,711 --> 00:57:47,505
You know, after my son
beat him up a couple of times,

954
00:57:47,589 --> 00:57:50,842
he couldn't even bring himself
to ride the bus that stops by my house.

955
00:57:55,180 --> 00:57:56,097
Oh.

956
00:57:59,392 --> 00:58:00,226
Hello, sir.

957
00:58:00,310 --> 00:58:03,813
Oh-seong, stay out of that gambling den.
This is your last warning.

958
00:58:04,856 --> 00:58:06,232
Bow to him, you idiot.

959
00:58:06,774 --> 00:58:10,320
- Show the man some respect!
- Ah, no, no. It's fine. It's fine.

960
00:58:10,403 --> 00:58:11,529
All right, gimme that.

961
00:58:13,907 --> 00:58:16,493
Oh God, that's heavy.

962
00:58:17,160 --> 00:58:19,704
Wow. Okay.

963
00:58:21,122 --> 00:58:22,248
Ah, this weighs a ton.

964
00:58:26,002 --> 00:58:27,170
Velvet antler.

965
00:58:27,253 --> 00:58:28,963
Goodness. Get that out of here.

966
00:58:29,047 --> 00:58:31,674
What the hell am I supposed
to do with that? You keep it.

967
00:58:31,758 --> 00:58:32,675
It's good for you.

968
00:58:33,176 --> 00:58:36,471
I'm just looking out for your health.
Is that so terrible?

969
00:58:40,725 --> 00:58:41,726
Take a look.

970
00:58:50,360 --> 00:58:54,906
I think that Choi Bool-am
is the TV actor I respect the most.

971
00:58:54,989 --> 00:58:57,575
He's always risking his life
to get the bad guy.

972
00:58:57,659 --> 00:59:00,161
Catching a petty thief
can't be so hard, can it?

973
00:59:06,584 --> 00:59:08,378
I'm Dodong-ri's Bu Sang-gil.

974
00:59:09,087 --> 00:59:11,548
You'll never get a safer bribe.
I guarantee you.

975
00:59:16,844 --> 00:59:20,348
Turns out, you're just as much
a father as any of us, Sang-gil.

976
00:59:20,848 --> 00:59:21,891
I'll be damned.

977
00:59:23,184 --> 00:59:25,853
Oh, please.
It's what a father would do for his child.

978
00:59:27,021 --> 00:59:29,649
I was a village chief,
a captain, and a father.

979
00:59:30,149 --> 00:59:34,153
And I have found
that being a father is the biggest loss.

980
00:59:35,822 --> 00:59:37,782
- Now say "ah."
- I'm fine, really.

981
00:59:37,865 --> 00:59:40,201
Come on, you look hungry.
Open up.

982
00:59:40,285 --> 00:59:43,037
- Fine.
- Hey, don't bite the hand that feeds you.

983
00:59:43,705 --> 00:59:47,542
When I listened to you refuse her
the money she needed to save her husband,

984
00:59:47,625 --> 00:59:50,336
any sentiment I had left for you

985
00:59:50,420 --> 00:59:52,463
<i>disappeared from my heart forever.</i>

986
00:59:52,547 --> 00:59:54,799
You like giving newspaper interviews, huh?

987
00:59:54,882 --> 00:59:57,802
Ah, hey, Sang-gil.
Just back up your car, and we can talk.

988
00:59:57,885 --> 00:59:59,220
If you're such a supercop,

989
00:59:59,304 --> 01:00:01,806
then why is Park Cheol-yong
still roaming the streets?

990
01:00:01,889 --> 01:00:04,392
Well, what gives you the right
to park your car like this

991
01:00:04,475 --> 01:00:05,810
in front of the police station?

992
01:00:06,311 --> 01:00:08,396
Oh yeah!

993
01:00:09,230 --> 01:00:11,482
You got your cut,
and now you're done with me, huh?

994
01:00:11,983 --> 01:00:13,735
Is that what's going on?

995
01:00:13,818 --> 01:00:15,528
Look, I promise you
I did the best I could.

996
01:00:15,612 --> 01:00:18,781
- Is this guy Jean Valjean or what?
- Jean Valjean? What are you saying?

997
01:00:18,865 --> 01:00:21,326
Why are you refusing
to finally hand him over to me?

998
01:00:21,409 --> 01:00:22,660
It's the global era.

999
01:00:22,744 --> 01:00:25,747
You have the Internet, everything,
so go find that lousy punk.

1000
01:00:25,830 --> 01:00:27,248
Sang-gil, are you drunk?

1001
01:00:27,332 --> 01:00:29,667
I've lost my wife and my fortune,
and I am losing my mind.

1002
01:00:29,751 --> 01:00:31,461
My life is spiraling out of control.

1003
01:00:31,544 --> 01:00:34,047
So if you don't want to be on the news
for the wrong reason,

1004
01:00:34,130 --> 01:00:38,635
either give me my money back with interest
or bring me Park Cheol-yong.

1005
01:00:38,718 --> 01:00:40,303
It is your choice, one or the other!

1006
01:00:40,386 --> 01:00:41,554
Interest?

1007
01:00:41,638 --> 01:00:43,056
Wow.

1008
01:00:43,139 --> 01:00:45,767
Dodong-ri's Bu Sang-gil
has sunk to a new low.

1009
01:00:48,061 --> 01:00:49,479
Dodong-ri's Bu Sang-gil.

1010
01:00:49,979 --> 01:00:51,981
To hell with that name! To hell with it!

1011
01:00:55,026 --> 01:00:59,072
How do you think they found Cheol-yong
through Joonggonara in the first place?

1012
01:00:59,155 --> 01:01:00,531
Isn't that funny?

1013
01:01:00,615 --> 01:01:02,825
Sang-gil and his little secrets.

1014
01:01:02,909 --> 01:01:05,328
- Always locking things up inside.
- What?

1015
01:01:05,828 --> 01:01:07,538
Like your ballroom dance class?

1016
01:01:11,834 --> 01:01:14,379
So when I snuck out to nightclubs,
I was just like you.

1017
01:01:14,462 --> 01:01:16,673
I had to. I couldn't breathe otherwise.

1018
01:01:17,256 --> 01:01:19,133
When I got home early in the morning,

1019
01:01:20,218 --> 01:01:23,971
I used to open the door slowly to see
if Dad was sleeping in the living room.

1020
01:01:24,722 --> 01:01:27,475
He didn't care enough about it
to stay awake for you.

1021
01:01:27,558 --> 01:01:29,018
Nuh-uh, he did.

1022
01:01:29,769 --> 01:01:31,145
One time, I saw him.

1023
01:01:31,813 --> 01:01:33,398
As soon as I opened the door,

1024
01:01:33,481 --> 01:01:36,776
he turned the TV off
and pretended he was asleep.

1025
01:01:37,944 --> 01:01:39,195
If you think about it…

1026
01:01:43,282 --> 01:01:45,535
Dad's actually a very timid man.

1027
01:01:45,618 --> 01:01:47,829
He yells a lot,
but if he thinks he'll lose,

1028
01:01:48,371 --> 01:01:49,997
he won't dare to put up a fight.

1029
01:01:51,541 --> 01:01:53,418
I think Dad was a little afraid

1030
01:01:54,168 --> 01:01:55,461
that, eventually,

1031
01:01:56,212 --> 01:01:57,547
everyone would leave him.

1032
01:02:02,009 --> 01:02:05,471
That man.
I can't stand when I see him.

1033
01:02:05,555 --> 01:02:07,306
I can't stand when I don't.

1034
01:02:14,480 --> 01:02:15,898
<i>Eventually,</i>

1035
01:02:15,982 --> 01:02:18,901
<i>time makes all things</i>
<i>into watercolor paintings.</i>

1036
01:02:19,652 --> 01:02:20,862
<i>It blurs spite.</i>

1037
01:02:22,530 --> 01:02:24,365
<i>It softens people's hearts.</i>

1038
01:02:25,575 --> 01:02:26,743
Bunch of ingrates.

1039
01:02:27,535 --> 01:02:28,578
I gave all of them my best,

1040
01:02:28,661 --> 01:02:30,913
but no one's ever
bought me something like that.

1041
01:02:31,622 --> 01:02:35,418
These days…
…I'm lucky to get a bag of rice.

1042
01:02:35,918 --> 01:02:37,170
Come to the restaurant tomorrow.

1043
01:02:37,879 --> 01:02:39,172
What, like I don't have plans?

1044
01:02:40,673 --> 01:02:42,049
There's a lot of places I could go.

1045
01:02:42,133 --> 01:02:45,136
Come on. Do it to help out your in-laws.

1046
01:02:45,720 --> 01:02:48,389
Once the show airs on TV,
it might get pretty busy.

1047
01:02:49,140 --> 01:02:50,641
I wanna be rich, too, one day.

1048
01:02:51,184 --> 01:02:52,018
Yeah?

1049
01:02:52,518 --> 01:02:55,480
Well, it's pretty nice
until people turn on you and take it.

1050
01:02:56,063 --> 01:02:58,816
In fact, I seriously doubt
you have what it takes to be rich.

1051
01:02:58,900 --> 01:03:00,818
You lack the mentality for it.

1052
01:03:00,902 --> 01:03:03,321
- Why can't you be nice for once?
- For once?

1053
01:03:03,404 --> 01:03:04,655
Are you coming by or not?

1054
01:03:07,283 --> 01:03:08,326
So you're saying

1055
01:03:09,619 --> 01:03:10,703
that you need me?

1056
01:03:12,789 --> 01:03:14,499
I'm saying it's your last chance.

1057
01:03:23,841 --> 01:03:26,344
<i>To a building in the woods</i>
<i>that all had abandoned,</i>

1058
01:03:28,554 --> 01:03:30,723
<i>eight dwarves began gathering.</i>

1059
01:03:47,073 --> 01:03:49,116
Hey, someone help me open this.

1060
01:03:49,200 --> 01:03:50,201
Here we go.

1061
01:03:52,495 --> 01:03:53,538
Eun-myeong, come help me.

1062
01:03:57,041 --> 01:03:59,627
<i>And finally, at long last,</i>

1063
01:04:01,003 --> 01:04:04,882
<i>the dark forest</i>
<i>was filled with the ringing of bells.</i>

1064
01:06:51,757 --> 01:06:56,887
"IF YOU CAN'T, JUST BACK DOWN.
WE'RE ALWAYS HERE FOR YOU."

